<item>
  <title>Advances in systematics of Mimosa (Fabaceae): phylogeny and biogeography of the Petiolovariabilis clade</title>
  <link>https://lsbjordao.github.io/posts/Petiolovariavilis-Clade/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<div class="quarto-figure quarto-figure-center">
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="https://lsbjordao.github.io/posts/Petiolovariavilis-Clade/image.webp" class="img-fluid quarto-figure quarto-figure-center figure-img" style="width:50.0%"></p>
</figure>
</div>
<p>This study presents a comprehensive analysis of the phylogeny and biogeography of the <em>Petiolovariabilis</em> clade within the genus <em>Mimosa</em> (Fabaceae). The authors used molecular data to reconstruct the evolutionary history of this group and to infer its biogeographic patterns.</p>
<p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1093/sysbio/syaa096">https://doi.org/10.1093/sysbio/syaa096</a></p>



 ]]></description>
