<item>
  <title>TypeTaxonScript: sugarifying and enhancing data structures in biological systematics and biodiversity research</title>
  <link>https://lsbjordao.github.io/posts/TypeTaxonScript/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<div class="quarto-figure quarto-figure-center">
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="https://lsbjordao.github.io/posts/TypeTaxonScript/image.png" class="img-fluid quarto-figure quarto-figure-center figure-img" style="width:50.0%"></p>
</figure>
</div>
<p>TypeTaxonScript is a framework for managing taxonomic data collaboratively. It allows users to create, edit, and share taxonomic information in a structured format.</p>
<p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1093/biomethods/bpae017">https://doi.org/10.1093/biomethods/bpae017</a></p>
<p>It is better read in PDF format, which can be downloaded from the link below.</p>
<p><a href="https://academic.oup.com/biomethods/article-pdf/9/1/bpae017/57136701/bpae017.pdf">https://academic.oup.com/biomethods/article-pdf/9/1/bpae017/57136701/bpae017.pdf</a></p>



 ]]></description>
